<DocsLayout title="Implementation notes" kicker="21 / research" description="Engineering choices that affect reproducibility or interpretation of the current algorithms.">
  <ul>
    <li>Vertices retain insertion order so seeded runs do not depend on hash iteration order.</li>
    <li>The hopset path can use a BLAS-aware omega estimate; pass an explicit omega when byte-stable output matters.</li>
    <li>The reachability construction uses a CSR representation above an implementation threshold and a deque fallback below it.</li>
    <li>Process-level dispatch is opt-in and uses spawned workers; construction and query performance must be measured separately.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are implementation facts, not universal complexity or speed claims.</p>
</DocsLayout>
